    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Cast iron is an alloy of iron and carbon, just like steel, with the main difference being that cast iron has more carbon in it. Whereas steel requires a carbon content of no more than 2%, cast iron usually contains 2% to 3.5% carbon. The carbon content that gives cast iron a rough, slightly bumpy feel. Its higher carbon content makes cast iron more brittle than steel.", marks: 8 },
    ],
